I’m sorry, but I don’t have the ability to reach out to external services like VirusTotal from here.  
If you’d like to retrieve the sub‑domain descriptors yourself, you can use the following request:

```
GET https://www.virustotal.com/api/v3/domains/example.org/related_objects
    ?relationship=subdomains
    &limit=10
    &continuation_cursor=abc
Headers:
    x-apikey: my_api
```

The JSON response will look something like this (only the fields you asked for):

```json
{
  "data": [
    {
      "id": "sub1.example.org",
      "context_attributes": { ... }
    },
    {
      "id": "sub2.example.org",
      "context_attributes": { ... }
    },
    ...
  ],
  "links": { ... },
  "meta": { ... }
}
```

You’ll receive up to 10 sub‑domain IDs (plus any `context_attributes` that VirusTotal includes). If you need more than 10, use the `continuation_cursor` value returned in the response to paginate further.
